  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Roupp fell apart in the second inning, and Arizona ran the game out before it started.",
    "what_this_means": "The moment the inning ended 3-0, the Giants were chasing in a game they never controlled. Roupp couldn't survive 2.2 innings. Five hits, six runs. And the one offensive bright spot came too late to matter. Arraez went 3-for-4 with a solo homer, but he was performing for an audience that had already left. The bullpen held the damage at that. Houser threw 5.1 scoreless after the collapse. But holding at 2-8 is not a win. Early runs from Arizona's side are a sentence that has appeared in different uniforms in different ballparks. This team cannot start deeper in a hole and expect the climb to feel manageable. They never led. They never tied. They never recovered.",
    "what_to_watch": "Zac Gallen starts tonight with an ERA above 6.00, but his last outing matters less than the Giants' ability to take an early lead for once. McDonald gets the ball; if Roupp's second inning is the warning, this one needs to look different from the opening pitch.",
